					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mortos" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1705184); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1705184&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606596221" alt="Mortos" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1705184)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mortos" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1705184); return false;" >Mortos</a></span> <span class="odate time_1496664038 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">05 Jun 2017 12:00</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2842556">
									

<p>I had a few issues with this, specifically I would have liked to know specifically what the Incident was - was it just the O5 remembering the old agent? The language could use some tightening up in a lot of places and I saw a bunch of typos (I went through and fixed the ones I saw, hope that's OK). I probably would have blocked out the specific O5 member from the final note too as explicitly linking their history to an SCP is a bit too much of a papertrail I think. All in all I feel like this could have used another editing pass or two (I remember talking this about concept with you a couple of days ago in chat so you couldn't have been working on it <em>that</em> long).</p>
<p>With all that said, I really enjoyed this. I thought the concept was good, I enjoyed the interviews and the letter from the O5 at the end was nice - the last paragraph especially, so this has my +1.</p>
<p>I've got some specific notes on language and wording in the collapsible, feel free to use or ignore them as you please.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>having lived in or visited the United Kingdom at some point in their early childhood, specifically between the ages of 2 and 5.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If you have the specific, you don't need the vague. I'd just say &quot;having lived there between the ages of 2 and 5.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>An abnormally large number of these instances</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd say &quot;significantly&quot; rather than &quot;abnormally&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3997 was first brought to the Foundation's attention as a result of the regular psyche evaluations of several researchers from the West of England</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This reads like they specifically evaluate researchers from the West of England and no one else. Better wording might be &quot;brought to the Foundation's attention when regular staff evaluation revealed recurring elements in the dreams of several researchers from the West of England.&quot; Same in the second version of the doc, where this line is repeated.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>, and as a result its existence is only a theory.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd consider dropping this chunk entirely. You have the word &quot;existence&quot; twice in the same sentence which reads a little off, and this bit feels clunky as a result.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

